#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:99
msgid ""
"What news search and AI assistants actually look for, and which setting "
"answers each of them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:120
msgid ""
"Ordinary SEO asks how to rank for a search people make again and again. News"
" is different. A story has hours, not months. Nobody searches for it before "
"it happens, and more and more readers never see a list of links, because "
"something answered them instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:121
msgid ""
"That splits the work in two. News SEO is about being found fast and trusted "
"by Google News and Discover. AI SEO is about being readable, attributable "
"and quotable by the assistants people ask instead of searching. They "
"overlap, but a site can be good at one and invisible in the other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:122
msgid ""
"Below: what each looks for, why, and where Ysgrif handles it. None of it is "
"a trick. It comes down to stating plainly, in a form machines can read, what"
" a good newsroom already does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:138
msgid "1. Speed, and how Google even learns a story exists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:140
msgid ""
"A normal page can wait days to be crawled. A story about this morning is "
"worthless by tomorrow, so what matters is whether Google finds it within "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:141
msgid ""
"Two things help, and they work together. A news sitemap is a short list of "
"only your recent stories, which Google News re-reads constantly instead of "
"crawling the whole site. A ping tells search engines the moment something is"
" published or corrected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:144
msgid ""
"A news sitemap lists your stories from the last two days, and nothing else, "
"so it is cheap to re-read often."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:145
msgid ""
"The sitemap address has to be submitted to Google Search Console once. "
"Nothing happens until it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:146
msgid ""
"Discover favours large images. Below about 1,200 pixels wide a story is "
"unlikely to be shown there at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:147
msgid ""
"A correction is news too. A story that changes should say so and be "
"announced again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:155
msgid "2. Who is publishing this, and why should anyone believe it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:157
msgid ""
"Publishers often skip this part and lose on it. Google does not judge a "
"story on its words alone; it judges the newsroom behind it. A site with no "
"named editor, no stated standards and no way to report a mistake looks, to a"
" machine, like a content farm, however good the journalism is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:158
msgid ""
"The same signals decide whether AI assistants name you as a source. An "
"assistant that cannot tell who stands behind a claim will quote someone who "
"can be identified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:161
msgid ""
"A real organisation: a name, a logo, an address, a way to be contacted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:162
msgid ""
"Real authors: a byline that links to a page saying who the person is and "
"what they cover, not “Admin”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:163
msgid ""
"Pages that say how you work: who runs the site, how it is funded, how you "
"check facts, how a reader reports an error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:164
msgid "Corrections shown openly rather than edited away quietly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:172
msgid "3. Structured data: saying it in a form machines cannot misread"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:174
msgid ""
"A machine reading your page sees text and guesses. Which line is the "
"headline? Which name is the author, and which is a person quoted in "
"paragraph four? Is that date when it was written or when it was updated? "
"Guesses go wrong often enough to matter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:175
msgid ""
"Structured data removes the guessing. It is a hidden, machine-readable "
"summary of the story (headline, author, dates, section, images, who and what"
" it is about) carried alongside the page. Google News and serious AI "
"crawlers read it rather than guess, so getting it right matters more than "
"anything else on the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:178
msgid ""
"A story marked as a news article, not as a blog post or an untyped page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:179
msgid "Published and updated dates that are both present and both honest."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:180
msgid ""
"Names tied to identities: a link saying which Wikidata entry, company or "
"official page a name refers to. Without one, a name is just two words."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:181
msgid ""
"One canonical address per story, so copies are not counted as rivals to the "
"original."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:189
msgid "4. AI assistants: two kinds of visitor, and why the difference matters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:191
msgid ""
"ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini and other AI engines visit news sites "
"for two different reasons. The commonest mistake is to treat them as one and"
" the same."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:192
msgid ""
"Some AI bots arrive because a reader has just asked a question, and they "
"answer it with a link to your story. Those visits send you readers; blocking"
" them turns traffic away. Others collect text to train a model. They give "
"you nothing directly, and whether to allow them is your own editorial and "
"commercial decision."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:193
msgid ""
"Ysgrif lists the two kinds of bots separately. The setup wizard offers the "
"middle course as its default: allow answers with a link, no training. That "
"is where most newsrooms want to land. But you can still set each crawler by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:196
msgid ""
"Being quotable: clear attribution, a visible publication date, claims that "
"stand on their own without the surrounding page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:197
msgid ""
"A plain-text version of a story, without the navigation and the design, is "
"far easier for an assistant to read correctly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:198
msgid ""
"llms.txt is a short, plain list of your latest stories, offered for "
"assistants to read quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:199
msgid ""
"Blocking everything does not make you neutral. It makes you absent from the "
"answers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:207
msgid "5. Why this is worth your afternoon"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:209
msgid ""
"For twenty years the deal was simple: write good news and get ranked for it "
"while collecting the clicks and readers' visits. That deal is being "
"rewritten. More and more questions are answered by AI on the search page or "
"inside the assistant itself. Readers may never arrive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/learn-seo.php:210
msgid ""
"You cannot opt out, but you can choose which side you are on. Sites named "
"and linked in those answers are ones that machines identify, date, attribute"
" and quote with confidence. That requires good structured data and a "
